        <!-- overview:begin -->

        ### Diagrams

        ![Logic block diagram](assets/diagrams/hi3535-logic.svg)

        ![Register blocks by function](assets/diagrams/hi3535-blocks.svg)

        ![Clock tree](assets/diagrams/hi3535-clocks.svg)

        ![Boot flow](assets/diagrams/hi3535-boot.svg)

        ![Video pipeline](assets/diagrams/hi3535-video.svg)

        ![Interrupt topology](assets/diagrams/hi3535-irq.svg)

        ![Reset tree](assets/diagrams/hi3535-resets.svg)

        ![Power domains](assets/diagrams/hi3535-power.svg)

        ![CRG register map](assets/diagrams/hi3535-crgmap.svg)

        ![bus clock domains](assets/diagrams/hi3535-bus.svg)

        ![IP edition per chip](assets/diagrams/hi3535-family.svg)

        ### Key specifications (data sheet chapter 1; the data sheet is Chinese, translated)

        | | Hi3535 V100 |
        |---|---|
        | CPU | dual Cortex-A9, up to 1 GHz; 32 KB L1 I + 32 KB L1 D per core, 256 KB L2 |
        | DDR | one 32-bit DDR3 controller, up to 800 MHz, up to 2 GB |
        | Decode | H.264 BP/MP/HP L5.0, MPEG4 SP/ASP, MJPEG/JPEG baseline |
        | Encode | H.264 BP/MP/HP L4.2, MJPEG/JPEG baseline |
        | Performance examples | 5x1080p@30 decode + 1x1080p@30 encode; 9x720p@30 decode + 1x1080p@30 encode; 24xD1@30 decode + 1x1080p@30 encode |
        | Video output | 1 HDMI 1.4, 1 VGA (up to 1920x1200@60), 1 BT.1120, 1 CVBS; three full-screen GUI layers (two HD, one SD) and a 128x128 cursor |
        | Audio | integrated audio codec, 2 I2S (1 in, 1 out), software codecs |
        | Network | 2 gigabit Ethernet (RGMII/RMII/MII, TOE) |
        | Peripherals | 2 SATA 3.0, 1 PCIe 2.0 / SATA 3.0 shared port (RC and endpoint), 4 UART (2 with four wires), IR, I2C, GPIO, 2 USB 2.0 host, 1 USB 3.0 host |
        | Flash | SPI NOR (1/2/4 bit, 2 CS, 32 MB each), 8-bit NAND (SLC/MLC, 1/4/8/24 bit ECC) with NAND boot |
        | On-chip memory | 4 KB BOOTROM, 10 KB SRAM |
        | Package | EDHS-PBGA, 23 x 23 mm, 0.8 mm pitch; 3.5 W typical; core 1.1 V, CPU 1.2 V (down to 1.1 V), I/O 3.3 V, DDR3 1.5 V |

        ### Boot (data sheet 1.3, Table 1-1)

        | BOOTROM_SEL | BOOT_SEL1 | BOOT_SEL0 | Boot mode |
        |---|---|---|---|
        | 1 | X | X | BOOTROM (serial download) |
        | 0 | 0 | 0 | external SPI flash |
        | 0 | 1 | 0 | external NAND flash |
        | 0 | 0 | 1 | slave mode: the CPU does not start; a master chip loads the boot program into this chip's DDR over PCIe and releases its reset |

        BOOTROM_SEL is multiplexed with pin MDCK, BOOT_SEL1 with VOU1120_DATA10 and BOOT_SEL0 with VOU1120_DATA7. With BOOTROM_SEL = 1 the BOOTROM starts the serial download; if the serial link times out it evaluates BOOT_SEL1/BOOT_SEL0 (00 = SPI flash, 10 = NAND flash).

        ### Chip ID

        | Chip | System controller ID registers (0xEE0 .. 0xEEC) | Value read as SC_SYSID |
        |---|---|---|
        | hi3535 | SYSID0..3 reset values from the RDL | 0x35350100 |

        The four 8-bit registers form the 32-bit chip ID (SYSID3 is the most significant byte). The values are the reset values of the register descriptions: one data sheet documents one ID for all chips it covers, so the chips of a shared data sheet are not distinguished here (the real value of each variant is not stated).

        ### Memory map notes (data sheet 1.3, Table 1-2)

        * 0x00000000-0x03FFFFFF (64 MB) is the boot window: it points to the BOOTROM while the remap is active and to the on-chip RAM (10 KB) after the remap is cleared; BOOTROM window 0x04000000 (4 KB implemented), RAM window 0x04010000.
        * Flash windows: NAND controller memory space 0x50000000-0x53FFFFFF (64 MB), SPI flash memory space 0x58000000-0x5BFFFFFF (64 MB).
        * PCIe: memory space 0x30000000-0x3FFFFFFF (256 MB), configuration space 0x40000000-0x4FFFFFFF (256 MB); controller registers at 0x20800000. In slave boot mode a master chip writes the boot program into this chip's DDR over PCIe (boot table).
        * DDR: 0x80000000-0xFFFFFFFF (2 GB window; one 32-bit DDR3 controller up to 2 GB).
        * Dual Cortex-A9: private region (SCU, GIC, timers, watchdogs) 0x20300000, L2 cache controller 0x20700000, ARM DEBUG 0x20400000-0x2051FFFF.
        * The DMAC window 0x10060000 (IRQ 46) is in the memory map but the data sheet has no DMAC chapter: no request-line table (see DMA).

        ### DMA request lines

        The memory map lists a DMAC at 0x10060000 and the interrupt table lists DMAC as interrupt 46, but the data sheet contains no DMAC register chapter and no request-line table, and the RDL does not model the block. The Hi3520D V100 has no DMAC at all and the later chips use the PL080-style block; nothing here is inferred for the Hi3535 beyond its presence in the map.

        ### Pin multiplexing summary (IOMUX at 0x200F0000)

        Generated from the pin mux registers of this description (register offsets are relative to the block base; the function lists are the value-ordered choices of each register). Pads that repeat a pattern in consecutive registers are merged into one row.

        | Pads | Mux register (offset from 0x200F0000) | Function choices (value 0, 1, ...) |
        |---|---|---|
        | VGA_HS | muxctrl_reg0 @0x000 | 0=VGA_HS / 1=GPIO6_6 |
        | VGA_VS | muxctrl_reg1 @0x004 | 0=VGA_VS / 1=GPIO6_7 |
        | RGMII0_RXDV | muxctrl_reg2 @0x008 | 0=RGMII0_RXDV / 1=GPIO8_7 |
        | RGMII0_RXD0 ... RGMII0_RXD3 (4) | muxctrl_reg3 ... muxctrl_reg6 @0x00C ... 0x018 | 0=RGMII0_RXD0 / 1=GPIO9_0 (first pad; others the same pattern with the pad's own number) |
        | RGMII0_TXD0 ... RGMII0_TXD3 (4) | muxctrl_reg7 ... muxctrl_reg10 @0x01C ... 0x028 | 0=RGMII0_TXD0 / 1=GPIO9_4 (first pad; others the same pattern with the pad's own number) |
        | RGMII0_RXCK | muxctrl_reg11 @0x02C | 0=RGMII0_RXCK / 1=GPIO8_0 |
        | RGMII0_TXEN | muxctrl_reg12 @0x030 | 0=RGMII0_TXEN / 1=GPIO8_1 |
        | RGMII0_TXCK | muxctrl_reg13 @0x034 | 0=RGMII0_TXCK / 1=GPIO8_2 |
        | RGMII0_TXCKOUT | muxctrl_reg14 @0x038 | 0=RGMII0_TXCKOUT / 1=GPIO8_3 / 2=RMII0_CLK |
        | RGMII0_CRS | muxctrl_reg15 @0x03C | 0=RGMII0_CRS / 1=GPIO8_4 |
        | RGMII0_COL | muxctrl_reg16 @0x040 | 0=RGMII0_COL / 1=GPIO8_5 |
        | RGMII0_RXER | muxctrl_reg17 @0x044 | 0=RGMII0_RXER / 1=GPIO8_6 |
        | RGMII1_RXDV | muxctrl_reg18 @0x048 | 0=RGMII1_RXDV / 1=GPIO10_7 |
        | RGMII1_RXD0 ... RGMII1_RXD2 (3) | muxctrl_reg19 ... muxctrl_reg21 @0x04C ... 0x054 | 0=RGMII1_RXD0 / 1=GPIO2_0 / 2=DDRPHY_DEBUG_OUT4 (first pad; others the same pattern with the pad's own number) |
        | RGMII1_RXD3 | muxctrl_reg22 @0x058 | 0=RGMII1_RXD3 / 1=GPIO2_3 |
