        Pad drive-strength and pull controls are in the separate pad control registers of the same description (not repeated here).

        ### Power, reset and system modes (data sheet 3.1, 3.2, 3.9)

        * Resets: same scheme as the Hi3520D V100: npor from the RSTN pin (low for more than 12 XIN cycles), global soft reset from the system controller (at least 360 system clock cycles), per-module soft resets in the PERI_CRG registers (hold-until-cleared). Slave boot mode keeps the CPU in reset (SYS_CTRL: cpu0 reset only valid in slave load mode, PERI_CRG description).
        * System modes: NORMAL (APLL enabled, ARM subsystem on the PLL), SLOW (APLL off, 24 MHz crystal), DOZE (APLL off, 46.875 kHz divided clock).
        * CPU frequency: PERI_CRG12[8] cpu_sc_sel (0 = APLL FOUTPOSTDIV, 1 = 750 MHz); dynamic frequency scaling by clock skipping: a9clk_skipcfg PERI_CRG10[24:20] (N = clock pulses removed per 32 cycles; with the 750 MHz source N = 1 gives 750 x 31 / 32 = 726.25 MHz) with the load strobe a9clk_loaden PERI_CRG10[25] (write the value, write loaden 0, then 1).
        * DDR source (slow mode only): PERI_CRG12[5:4] ddr_sc_sel (400 / 324 / 300 MHz or APLL FOUT1PH0); bus source (slow mode only): PERI_CRG12[2:0] bus_sc_sel (hpaxi 324 or 250 MHz, mdaaxi 324 or 250 MHz, sysaxi 250 or 200 MHz).
        * Six PLLs: APLL PERI_CRG0/1, BPLL PERI_CRG2/3, VPLL0 PERI_CRG4/5, VPLL1 PERI_CRG6/7, VPLL2 PERI_CRG72/73, EPLL PERI_CRG8/9; VCO must be 600 MHz to 2.4 GHz.
        * The data sheet has no separate power-domain table.

